note: every kind mistake with maps
let ages be a map of "Paris" to 19, "Junie" to 24.
let scores be a list of 72 and 95.
say the value for 3 in ages
say the value for "Ada" in scores
set the value for "Ada" in ages to "old"
say the value for "Ada" in ages, or "none"
if scores has 72, say "yes"
if ages has yes, say "yes"
say the number of entries in scores
say the keys of scores
say the values of 7
remove 95 from scores
remove 3 from ages
let mixed be a map of "a" to 1, 2 to 3
let mixed values be a map of "a" to 1, "b" to "two"
let flags be a map of yes to 1
let twice be a map of "tea" to 2, "tea" to 3
let twice numbers be a map of 1 to 2, 1.0 to 3
for each name in ages:
    say name
for each a1 and b1 in scores:
    say a1
set the value for "x" in scores to 1
add 1 to the value for 3 in ages
say ages plus 1
say ages is greater than ages
say ages as a number
let other be an empty map from numbers to numbers
if ages is other, say "same"
say length of ages
say ages contains "Paris"
let graph be an empty map from text to lists of numbers
add 5 to the value for "a" in graph
add "x" to the value for "a" in graph
set ages to graph
say "x" followed by ages followed by graph
say ages and other
